===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[after]]-[[clap]]}}

# {{1811}} A [[problem]] or [[danger]] that arises after a [[threat]] is supposed to have passed.

====Quotations====
* '''1782''', ''letter from [[w:Benjamin Franklin|Benjamin Franklin]] to Robert Morris, 9 January, 1782'', published in ''The Complete Works of Benjamin Franklin: volume VII'' (John Bigelow, [[editor]]; ISBN-13: 9781443755863) in 2008:
*: Sir:&mdash;I have long feared that by our continually worrying the ministry here with successive after-clap demands for more and more money, we should at length tire out their patience. 

